  "rootCause": "getAccessSnapshot fenced featureRevision across two awaited liveness lookups; normal next_sequence metadata mutation increments that revision. Its benign exception, and provider/storage exceptions generally, were swallowed as stable denial by authorizeEvent and validateJournalMessage. Replay consequently committed a cursor beyond the authorized skipped row.",
  "correction": {
    "coherentSnapshot": "Capture identity generation/canonical name, await one real liveness read, then authoritative account/version/network-ban/scope checks; enforce identity generation fence; evaluate all local members, aggregated effective role modes, bans/mutes/quiets/read-only/channel modes/custom permissions synchronously using shared helpers. Ordinary metadata revisions can change during awaits without dropping events.",
    "denialContract": "Existing F3 standard Error-message contract explicitly recognizes SESSION_EXPIRED401, SCOPE_FORBIDDEN403 and NETWORK_BANNED403, including DO RPC. Only these are false authorization results; current generation mismatch409 and unexpected SQL/provider failures propagate. Conversation payload suppresses only actual MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND404; stable deletion/redaction still returnsfalse.",
    "recoveryContract": "Operational errors propagate through polling to existing close1008/recovery-required behavior; stored account-bound position remains6, both journal records persist, explicit replay from last acknowledged position returns both private IDs exactly once and in order; public outsider control and fresh authorized delivery remain live."
  },
  "privacyAndRevocation": "Secret outsider receives neither private ID in race/error/recovery cases; actual IRC ban applied during held liveness suppresses both private events, real ban removal restores positive delivery, and the existing in-flight removal plus credential-revocation test passes. No role policy or authorization mock changes.",
